Z||000004||Bazooka||09-29-2001||05:29 PM||||This 6 cylinder engine builder from Aystralia is turning 10.1's in the 1/4. Here's a posting from the Australian Fiero Shop Forum at  <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au/cgi-bin/ikonboard/ikonboard.cgi" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop.com.au/cgi-bin/ikonboard/ikonboard.cgi</A> <BR>******************************<BR>Jim Davis  <BR>Administrator              <BR>Hey cool. Thats sounds like a cheaper way to do a respray hey. I keep looking at my poor Fiero sitting there, heaps of panels missing, can't drive it anymore. All this after pouring over $32,000 into it. <P>But I think I have found an engine conversion for it finally. A supercharged buick 3.8 ltr crate motor put in by a guy that does nothing but V6 conversions over here. Hard part to swallow, $10,000 cost. Ouch. Fieros are not a cheap hobby here. On the up side though his car that is 200kgs heavier than the Fiero runs 10.1 at the strip with the same engine. Am hoping for 9.9s in the Fiero  <BR>-----<BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and fast cars. I guess I wasted the rest.  <BR>******************************<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pontiacs4me:<BR><B>12.92 is pretty fast, can any body else challenge that?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>******************************<BR>||||reg||1
